    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "「凡有残疾，或有甚么恶病的牛羊，你都不可献给耶和华―你的　神，因为这是耶和华―你　神所憎恶的。",
      "en": "You must not sacrifice to him[NOTE:1] a bull or sheep that has a blemish or any other defect, because that is considered offensive[NOTE:2] to the Lord your God.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “to the Lord your God.” See note on “he” in 16:1.",
        "The Hebrew word תּוֹעֵבָה (toʿevah, “an abomination”; cf. NAB) describes persons, things, or practices offensive to ritual or moral order. See M. Grisanti, NIDOTTE 4:314-18; see also the note on the word “abhorrent” in Deut 7:25."
